{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RESOLVED for the immediate blockage, by the operator's chosen option: pin this gate environment.\n\nCHANGE: Gerrit 1355, MERGED (`846b: pin the maintainer gate environment`), one file, +23 lines —\n`.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` gains env_id `ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5` with the\npublic half of this environment's op-cert key\n(`ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBJYVGrlY0lry1wXJUH16LysXt4NezYJ98El+EK1yuo3 rebar-opcert`).\nLLM-Review +1, Verified +1, submitted; `main` is 75cdfec3572 and the pin reads back from it.\n\nERA START IS NOT BACKDATED. `added_at_log_position` is `1785855397918577001-d97467a4-…`, the\ntickets-branch tip at the moment of pinning — deliberately NOT reached back over the certs this\nenvironment had already written. Those stay outside the era and had to be re-signed, which is\nexactly story 4214's anti-backdating property and the reason the era model uses tickets-branch log\npositions rather than main SHAs. Re-signing was free (`sign-review` replays the recorded\nREVIEW_RESULT sidecar; no LLM re-run).\n\nVERIFIED BY RUNNING THE GATE'S OWN CLASSIFIER, not by pushing and hoping:\n    >>> classify_plan_review_attestation(\"129e-2d88-cce2-492c\", repo_root=\".\")\n    {'verdict': 'stale-head', 'reason': 'attestation is stale (unscoped; signed at 75cdfec357…)'}\n    >>> bucket_for_verdict('stale-head')\n    'accepted'\nBefore the pin this same call returned `mismatch` (\"signing environment … is not pinned\"), whose\nbucket BLOCKS. After the pin the keyring lookup succeeds, so the classifier proceeds past the\nkeyring arm to the drift arm — and `stale-head` is one of the arms the gate explicitly ACCEPTS\n(\"Code drift is ACCEPTED … punishing them would make the gate flaky-by-design\"). That is the\nmechanism, confirmed locally before any CI spend.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT GRANT, recorded because it is the security question this ticket turns on: the\npin makes this environment's plan-review certs VERIFIABLE. It does not widen who may VOTE.\n`LLM-Review` and `Verified` are still cast only by the bots, so a change still cannot self-approve;\nwhat changed is that a plan review this environment genuinely ran is no longer rejected purely on\nprovenance. The loader still refuses an unknown env (checked: a bogus env_id returns None).\n\nSTILL OPEN — this ticket is NOT fully discharged by the pin, and should stay open for the rest:\n  * AC1/AC3 remain unmet in the general case. Pinning one maintainer environment unblocks THIS\n    maintainer; it does not give an arbitrary contributor a path, and the failure message still\n    does not name a remedy — an author who hits it must still reverse-engineer\n    trusted_environments.yaml and the compose file to learn why a PASSING plan review was\n    rejected. Both of those were the substance of AC2/AC3.\n  * The deeper gap is unchanged: the op-cert service has no client in this repo and never persists\n    what it signs, so \"get a prod-attested plan review\" is still not an executable instruction.\n  * Worth deciding separately: whether the not-pinned arm should be ADVISORY when NO developer\n    environment is pinnable, so the gate degrades to a warning instead of an unconditional block\n    the first time anyone new hits it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785858232979672001,"uuid":"9df4338e-5188-4155-ad8e-368eeac09191"}